(1. Definition of Deadlock) Tj
/F2 11 Tf
0 -20 Td
(A deadlock is a situation where a set of processes are blocked because each) Tj
0 -16 Td
(process is holding a resource and waiting for another resource held by another) Tj
0 -16 Td
(process in the set. None of the processes can run, release resources, or be awakened.) Tj
/F1 14 Tf
0 -35 Td
(2. Coffman's Four Necessary Conditions) Tj
/F2 11 Tf
0 -20 Td
(Deadlock can arise if and only if all four conditions hold simultaneously:) Tj
0 -18 Td
(  1. Mutual Exclusion: At least one resource must be held in non-shareable mode.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(  2. Hold and Wait: A process must be holding at least one resource and waiting) Tj
0 -16 Td
(     for additional resources held by other processes.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(  3. No Preemption: Resources cannot be preempted; only released voluntarily.) Tj
0 -18 Td
(  4. Circular Wait: A closed chain of processes exists where each process holds) Tj
0 -16 Td
(     one resource and waits for the next in the sequence.) Tj
